{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Refined the recovery-authority question from source reading before building its probe: a prepare reply whose Ballot differs from lastTriedBallot returns before being appended to lb.prepareReplies, so higher-ballot rejections never count toward SlowQuorumSize, no sub-case is selected at all, and the recovering replica emits no further message. This changes what the probe must observe (repeated identical prepares with no follow-up message, not a NOOP phase-1 restart).\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n  {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@k-prepare-nack-not-counted\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"In handlePrepareReply a reply whose Ballot differs from lb.lastTriedBallot increments lb.nacks and returns before the reply is appended to lb.prepareReplies, and the sub-case dispatch is guarded by len(lb.prepareReplies) >= SlowQuorumSize(); the only repair on the nack path (makeBallot plus a fresh bcastPrepare) is executed only while r.IsLeader is true.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Recovery where the replicas that answer the Prepare have a stored bal above the recovering replica's fixed tried ballot, so every answer is a rejection rather than a matching-ballot reply (epaxos/epaxos.go:1204-1235, with epaxos/epaxos.go:439-451 and 1216-1235).\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\", \\\"s-makeballot\\\", \\\"s-isleader-default\\\", \\\"s-betheleader\\\"]},\n  {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@k-fixed-recovery-ballot\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"makeBallot assigns the instance owner the ballot equal to its own replica id and any other recovering replica id+N, and advances it in steps of N only while r.IsLeader is true and the candidate is below maxRecvBallot; epaxos.New hardcodes IsLeader false and only the exported BeTheLeader RPC sets it, which the master invokes for the replica it designates.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Any startRecoveryForInstance call in the captured snapshot, including repeat calls from executeCommands after COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD (epaxos/epaxos.go:439-451, 1127-1150, 149-165, 1121-1125).\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s-makeballot\\\", \\\"s-decl-recovery\\\", \\\"s-isleader-default\\\", \\\"s-betheleader\\\"]}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"f47677cc0dd94647aa374fc84b1e6b8e-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"makeBallot gives every non-designated replica a fixed recovery ballot (r.Id for the instance owner, r.Id+N otherwise), so a recovery whose accepting peers have a higher stored bal is rejected on every attempt: each reply returns before the quorum append, no sub-case is dispatched, no further message is emitted, and the periodic retry repeats the identical Prepare ballot; only r.IsLeader (set by the master's BeTheLeader RPC) lets the ballot climb above maxRecvBallot, after which the same call joins the higher ballot and reaches the sub-case dispatch.\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Whether two consecutive startRecoveryForInstance calls on a non-designated replica emit the identical Prepare ballot while every matching reply carries the peers' higher stored bal and the replica emits no PreAccept, Accept or Commit for that instance, and whether invoking the target's own BeTheLeader then produces a Prepare ballot above maxRecvBallot that the peers join (producing a matching reply and a dispatched sub-case).\\\"}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('draft/update6.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update6.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
